1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,400
Here is agrisim running live on a Windows laptop,

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,387
from one command to a field map you can explore.

3
00:00:07,483 --> 00:00:11,589
One command runs a whole survey: our strategy, planned survey,

4
00:00:11,589 --> 00:00:12,517
on seed seven.

5
00:00:12,517 --> 00:00:14,106
It prints the map error,

6
00:00:14,106 --> 00:00:17,947
how well the map finds the dry cells, the distance driven,

7
00:00:17,947 --> 00:00:19,536
and zero plant contacts.

8
00:00:19,536 --> 00:00:22,715
The same seed gives the same numbers every time.

9
00:00:23,817 --> 00:00:24,582
Add --view,

10
00:00:24,582 --> 00:00:28,551
and the same survey opens as a 3D replay in your browser.

11
00:00:28,551 --> 00:00:32,798
The intro panel says what you are looking at, in plain words.

12
00:00:33,884 --> 00:00:36,995
The robot drives only in the lanes. When it stops,

13
00:00:36,995 --> 00:00:40,854
the six bars at the top right follow the probe: lower, insert,

14
00:00:40,854 --> 00:00:41,352
measure,

15
00:00:41,352 --> 00:00:43,779
pull out through the brushes, blow dry,

16
00:00:43,779 --> 00:00:45,148
and check it is clean.

17
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:47,649
When the value comes in,

18
00:00:47,649 --> 00:00:50,449
a ripple in the reading's colour marks the spot,

19
00:00:50,449 --> 00:00:51,324
a flag goes up,

20
00:00:51,324 --> 00:00:53,482
and the map fades to its new picture.

21
00:00:54,584 --> 00:00:56,129
Press D for the drone view,

22
00:00:56,129 --> 00:00:59,448
a camera that circles high above the rover while it works.

23
00:01:00,550 --> 00:01:03,384
The time bar shows the whole mission at once.

24
00:01:03,384 --> 00:01:04,896
Every tick is a reading,

25
00:01:04,896 --> 00:01:06,345
coloured like its flag.

26
00:01:06,345 --> 00:01:08,361
Point at it to preview a moment,

27
00:01:08,361 --> 00:01:11,259
or jump from stop to stop with the arrow keys.

28
00:01:12,350 --> 00:01:13,015
From above,

29
00:01:13,015 --> 00:01:15,013
the ground shows the robot's map.

30
00:01:15,013 --> 00:01:17,434
Switch to the real moisture to judge it,

31
00:01:17,434 --> 00:01:18,766
then to the map error,

32
00:01:18,766 --> 00:01:20,158
and to the uncertainty,

33
00:01:20,158 --> 00:01:22,398
which is lowest next to each reading.

34
00:01:23,484 --> 00:01:27,613
The field from above shows the route and every reading. Click one,

35
00:01:27,613 --> 00:01:29,740
and the replay jumps to that stop,

36
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:32,493
with the same reading ringed in the 3D view.

37
00:01:32,493 --> 00:01:35,371
The map error chart falls as readings come in,

38
00:01:35,371 --> 00:01:37,436
and plants touched stays at zero.

39
00:01:38,483 --> 00:01:40,349
This survey has a rain shower.

40
00:01:40,349 --> 00:01:42,215
The time bar shows it in blue,

41
00:01:42,215 --> 00:01:44,143
and a note says when it starts.

42
00:01:44,143 --> 00:01:46,818
Rain makes earlier readings go out of date,

43
00:01:46,818 --> 00:01:51,731
so planned survey drives on rather than probe soil the rain is about to change.

44
00:01:52,817 --> 00:01:54,815
The same replay works on a phone,

45
00:01:54,815 --> 00:01:57,480
with one panel at a time above the controls:

46
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:58,813
what is happening now,

47
00:01:58,813 --> 00:02:00,085
the field from above,

48
00:02:00,085 --> 00:02:01,478
and the ground colours.

49
00:02:02,583 --> 00:02:06,076
And agrisim bench compares strategies on the same fields,

50
00:02:06,076 --> 00:02:09,324
with ninety five percent intervals, from one command.

51
00:02:12,817 --> 00:02:14,063
Try it yourself.

52
00:02:14,063 --> 00:02:15,699
Install with uv sync,

53
00:02:15,699 --> 00:02:18,193
then run one survey with --view.
